A two-provider dependency cycle whose edges are satisfied through the value/pointer
bridge: MakeA consumes *B and MakeB consumes *A, each produced (as B / A) by the
other and bridged. The cycle diagnostic names each consumer’s declared type (*B,
*A), matching the source, and marks the bridged edge, rather than naming the
produced dual.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrDependencyCycle
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app

type A struct{}
type B struct{}

//plumb:build
func MakeA(b *B) A { return A{} }

//plumb:build
func MakeB(a *A) B { return B{} }
